[E0425] Error: `Handle` is a C type whose contents are not known, and this needs the size of `Handle`
    ╭─[ err/488_the_size_of_an_opaque_type_argument/main.wip:11:25 ]
    │
 11 │ fn sized<T>(): size_t = c::sizeOf<T>()
    │                         ───────┬──────
    │                                ╰──────── needs how large a `Handle` is
    │
 14 │     val size = sized<Handle>()
    │                ───────┬───────
    │                       ╰───────── `sized<Handle>` is made here
    │
    │ Help: a pointer to one is written `ptr<Handle>`, which a generic takes as `ptr<T>`
    │
    │ Note: an opaque C type says only that the type exists; how large one is, and what is in it, are C's business
────╯
